# ---------- Stormwind -> Redridge ----------
T 1666 @ Elwynn Forest, 84.6, 69.4 | From the Dwarven District leave Stormwind by the main gate and follow the road east through Goldshire to the Eastvale Logging Camp. Marshal Haggard stands at the house on the east side of the camp
A 1667 | Marshal Haggard
C 1667 @ Elwynn Forest, 89.4, 79.0 | Dead-Tooth Jack's camp is south-east of Eastvale, in the corner of Elwynn south of the road, close to the Redridge border. Kill Jack (level 11) and the Defias with him, loot Dead-tooth's Key from him and open the strongbox in the camp for Marshal Haggard's Badge
T 1667 | Marshal Haggard, back at Eastvale. This ends the level 10 warrior chain
A 244 | Back on the road, east to the Three Corners crossroads just inside Redridge. Guard Parker walks the road there.
F Lakeshire @ Redridge Mountains, 25.5, 59.4 | Follow the road north-east to Lakeshire. Ariena Stormfeather, the gryphon master, stands on the south side of the bridge. Redridge Mongrels (15-16) and Great Goretusks sit next to the road: leave them for now.
T 244 | Deputy Feldon, a few steps from the gryphon master
A 246 | Deputy Feldon
A 98407 @ Redridge Mountains, 25.6, 59.9 | Deputy Feldon: Show of Force (new in Forever)
A 3741 | Shawn, a child standing at the lake by the bridge (24.2, 53.6)
A 125 | Cross the bridge. Foreman Oslow stands at its north end.
A 118 | Verner Osgood, close to the bridge on the town side
A 120 | Magistrate Solomon in the town hall
A 127 | Dockmaster Baren on the dock in front of the town
A 129 | Darcy, the waitress in the inn
T 65 | Wiley the Black, upstairs in the inn. Do not take his follow-up (The Defias Brotherhood, back to Westfall).
A 92 | Chef Breanna, in the house west of the inn

# ---------- Lake Everstill ----------
C 3741 | Glinting Mud lies under water along the lake shore on both sides of the bridge (spots between 14 and 33, 51-56). Open the piles until one holds Hilary's Necklace.
C 125 @ Redridge Mountains, 36.4, 54.7 | Swim east from the bridge. The Sunken Chest with Oslow's Toolbox lies on the lake bottom. Murlocs (17-20) swim around it: kill what comes at you before you dive, and keep the fish they drop (Spotted Sunfish for Selling Fish).
T 3741 | Hilary, the girl next to Shawn
T 125 | Foreman Oslow
A 89 | Foreman Oslow

# ---------- Gnolls north of town ----------
C 89 @ Redridge Mountains, 24.0, 34.8 | The data lists the gnolls north of Lakeshire as the source of Iron Pikes and Iron Rivets: Redridge Brutes (17-18) in the camps around 24, 35 and Redridge Mystics (18-19) a little further north. Take the path north out of town. Pull one camp member at a time and kill the Mystics first: they cast, so interrupt them with Shield Bash if you carry a shield. If two come, kill the weaker one first or back off down the path. Do not go deeper than you need: Bashers (19-20) are behind them. Great Goretusks on the way drop snouts for the goulash.

# ---------- Gnolls and beasts south of the lake ----------
C 246,98407 @ Redridge Mountains, 20.0, 70.0 | Cross the bridge again and work the gnoll camps south and south-west of Lakeshire, toward Three Corners. Kill 10 Redridge Mongrels (15-16) and 6 Redridge Poachers (16-17, mostly in the southern camps around 29, 80), and every Redridge Thrasher (14-15) you see until you have 5 Spiked Collars. Poachers shoot: run up to them. Gnolls run at low health: finish them fast or slow them if you can, they bring friends. Tarantulas (15-16) and Great Goretusks (16-17) live between the camps: kill them as you go for 5 Crisp Spider Meat and 5 Great Goretusk Snouts (Redridge Goulash).
T 129 | Guard Parker at Three Corners
A 130 | Guard Parker
C 127 @ Redridge Mountains, 43.7, 69.2 | 10 Spotted Sunfish from murlocs. Murloc Shorestrikers (16-17) on the south shore of the lake around 44, 69 are the easiest; Minor Tidecallers and Flesheaters (17-19) live further along the shore and in the water. This is a level 21 quest: pull single murlocs from the edge of a camp, kill Tidecallers first (they heal: interrupt the cast with Shield Bash if you carry a shield) and finish every murloc fast or slow it if you can, because they run and bring friends. Keep every Murloc Fin you loot: Dockmaster Baren asks for 8 of them in the next segment. The condors for the goulash are next.
C 92 @ Redridge Mountains, 47.7, 56.9 | Redridge Goulash: the 5 Tough Condor Meat come from Dire Condors (18-19), which fly over the hills south and east of the lake, close to the murloc shore. Fight them one at a time with full health. If you still miss Crisp Spider Meat or Goretusk Snouts, Tarantulas and Great Goretusks are around Three Corners and all along the road back to Lakeshire.

